# Regression test: a bare (unannotated) local assigned from a call to a
# `'shared`-returning function -- `let s = makeShared()`, no explicit
# `Counter'shared` annotation -- never got its qualifier inferred at all, so
# passing it to a `'shared`-typed parameter re-wrapped it a second time
# (`Arc::new(s.clone())` on top of `s`'s own already-`Arc<Counter>`
# representation) -- a confirmed E0308 ("expected `Counter`, found
# `Arc<Counter>`").
#
# Root cause: `infer_qualifiers.rs`'s pre-pass that recognizes "this bare local
# comes from a lock-qualified-returning function call" (`collect_actor_lets` /
# `expr_returns_actor_qual`, feeding `infer_local_actor_vars`) only checked
# `'actor`/`'guard` return types, never `'shared` -- so `s`'s candidate set
# never got the early single-candidate narrowing `'actor`/`'guard` locals get,
# and the later call-site-demand signal alone leaves 3 candidates
# (`{Inline, Owned, Shared}`, see `coercible_from`), which the generic
# size-based fallback resolved to `Inline` instead of `Shared`.
# `emit_let.rs`'s own `'shared` codegen arm then never recognized `s` as
# already wrapped (unlike its `'actor`/`'guard` siblings, which already
# consulted `inferred_qualifiers` for exactly this reason) and wrapped it a
# second time.
#
# Fixed by a `'shared` counterpart pre-pass (`infer_local_shared_vars`,
# `src/transpiler/infer_qualifiers.rs`) that resolves such a local straight to
# `Shared` (unambiguous, unlike the `{Actor, Guard}` pair), and by teaching
# `emit_let.rs`'s `'shared` arm to also check `inferred_qualifiers` before
# deciding a value needs wrapping.
struct Counter:
    var int value = 0

Counter'shared makeShared():
    Counter(4)

def useShared(Counter'shared c):
    print "shared={c.value}"

def main():
    let s = makeShared()
    useShared(s)
    useShared(s)
    print "s={s.value}"
